      "state": "COMMENTED",
      "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nExpands standalone installation guidance and updates release messaging for the local brain distribution.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Adds cold-start installation, verification, refresh, query, and privacy guidance.\n- Updates release claims with benchmark and replay-lab evidence.\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 2 out of 2 changed files in this pull request and generated 3 comments.\n\n| File | Description |\n| ---- | ----------- |\n| `docs/getting-started.md` | Adds the standalone setup and first-run guide. |\n| `docs/release_press_release.md` | Refines release claims and evidence summaries. |\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suppressed comments (3)</summary>\n\n**docs/getting-started.md:51**\n* The brain's existing `v0.1.0` tag predates the Graph rename: its refresh path invokes `entire sem` and its plugin manifest requires `sem`. Installing that tag alongside a future/current `entire-graph` provider will not produce the documented `entire graph` integration. The brain must be re-tagged from the Graph-based code, or this guide must use a compatible version pair.\n```\ngo install github.com/ashtom/entire-brain/cmd/entire-brain@v0.1.0\n```\n**docs/release_press_release.md:145**\n* This repeats the unresolved assertion that both tagged repositories are aligned. The retained `entire-graph` `v0.1.0` tag is the legacy `entire-sem` provider and the retained brain tag consumes `entire sem`, not the Graph command documented by this PR. Do not mark the release checklist item shipped/aligned until replacement tags are available.\n```\n  harnessing, eval harness, benchmark harness. Both repos tagged `v0.1.0`,\n  aligned.\n```\n**docs/getting-started.md:76**\n* This source-install pair is not compatible or reproducible: the provider's `v0.1.0` checkout builds and installs `entire-sem`, while the unpinned brain checkout uses current `main` and its installer expects the sibling to provide `entire graph`. The final `doctor` therefore fails, and future changes to `main` also change what this supposedly versioned procedure installs. Pin both repositories to newly aligned Graph-based tags.\n```\ngit clone --branch v0.1.0 https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph.git\ngit clone https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain.git\n```\n</details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n\ud83d\udca1 <a href=\"/entireio/entire-brain/new/main?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.",
